    "story": "His father taught him to shoot squirrels with the same rule the sergeant teaches now: the shot you hurry belongs to nobody. Through the notch the world narrows to a fence rail's width — a road, a hedge, and men his age learning the same patience from the other side of both. He has time to wonder whether the one settling in over there also hunts squirrel, also writes his name inside his hat so they'll know. Then the wondering is a luxury, and the front sight is the whole of philosophy, and his finger makes its own decision.",
