    "story": "From behind, the regiment is all backs and he is the smallest of them, and nobody out here mistakes that for the least of them. The drum hangs on men twice his size on the march, but the calls live in his hands, and when the column halts the officers look for the small back in the crowd the way you look for a clock in a station. Doing his part was never the question put to him. The question was whether the part would wait until he grew into it. It would not. So he grew faster.",
