    "story": "The coat was issued to a man with a black beard and opinions about how the war would go, and both have since been revised. He has let the seams out twice and the certainties out oftener. What the uniform knows now that it didn't then: that a collar can hold a man up or wear him down, and the difference is mostly a matter of years. People ask why he doesn't take the newer coat the quartermaster keeps offering. He has buried friends in older ones. A man keeps the coat that knows him.",
