    "story": "The proposition, as the man across from him laid it out, had money in it, and a horse, and glory itemized like a bill of sale. He holds the revolver low and easy, the way a man holds a door shut — not a threat, exactly; a clarification — while he does the arithmetic that doesn't appear in the offer: a crop in the ground, a mother alone with the winter coming, and a signature that turns a man into a number other men get to spend. He hasn't said no. That's what keeps the other man talking. He hasn't said yes, either. That's what the revolver is for — making sure the thinking takes as long as it takes.",
