    "story": "Business, in a town the war keeps visiting, is mostly the art of still being open. He sells to soldiers who pay in promises and to officers who pay in coin and to widows who pay in neither and are served first anyway, a policy he does not advertise and would deny under oath. The armies take turns owning the street outside his door. He has learned to stock for both and pray for neither, and to keep his opinions where he keeps his good ledger: out of sight, in a drawer, under the counter of his face.",
