    "story": "Nobody in camp knows yet whether he is selling something or inspecting something, and he is in no hurry to relieve them of the suspense. The bag has been in a hundred camps and holds, depending on the camp, tonics, tintypes, official papers, or opinions about the general's dispositions, which he will share at the price of a meal. He travels because the war is the largest gathering of customers, mourners, and gossips in the history of the republic, and a man with a bag and a clean collar can be all three professions before supper. The tents will decide what he is by dark. They always do.",
