    "story": "The words are still arriving when the picture catches him — you can see them landing one by one. The farm is sold. The regiment is renumbered. The leave that was promised is un-promised, by a man in an office who has never had to say it to a face. He is doing the thing a man does before he decides what to feel: arguing with the messenger's arithmetic, hand on his hip like he can hold himself in place by main force. Regret and disbelief are only the first two stations. The train runs all night. He has a ticket he never bought.",
