    "story": "Peace, out here, is not the end of the war. It's a hole in it — twenty minutes wide, grass underneath, and a man flat on his back in the middle of it with his hands behind his head like the whole thing was his idea. He is not asleep. Asleep would waste it. He is inventorying the sky, the grass smell, the exact weight of nothing being required of him, storing it against the bugle the way you store water against a dry march. The men stepping around him don't begrudge it. His turn on the grass means their turn is coming, and hope, in this army, is mostly a roster.",
