    "story": "The other side's gun spoke first — that's the etiquette out here, an argument conducted in iron at a mile's distance. Answering it is not temper; it's grammar. Sponge, charge, shot, ram, prime: the crew runs the sentence by hand while the chief watches the far tree line for the punctuation of their last reply. The village green has hosted weddings within living memory. The church bell has opinions about all of this that it will keep until Sunday. For now the argument continues, each side correcting the other's aim in smoke, and the crew's whole world is the next round and the rhythm that loads it.",
