    "story": "The order to advance doesn't travel by bugle out here; it travels by throat — man to man down the line, each one cupping his hands and spending his voice like ammunition. By the time it reaches the end it has been shouted by fifty men and belongs to all of them, which is as it should be: they're the ones who'll be walking it. The colors lift. The ranks settle their rifles and their faces into the arrangement they use for being seen by history, and the whole body of them leans, the way a field of grain leans, one degree toward the enemy. Glory is the word the newspapers will use. The men use a shorter one: forward.",
