    "story": "The yell is not for the enemy. Let them make of it what they can. The yell is for the man next to you and the man you were a minute ago, sitting behind the fence rail doing the arithmetic of survival. It says the arithmetic is finished. They come over the rail at the pace of a debt being collected, rifles leveled, the old officer's sword out in front like a compass needle that only points one way. Ten steps in, there's no thinking left in it at all — just breath, noise, and the ground arriving faster than it has any right to. That's the secret the yell was keeping: it isn't courage. It's the sound of men outrunning their own fear, together, at a sprint.",
