    "story": "Motivation, the colonel has learned, is not a speech. Speeches are for courthouses. Out here it is a fence between you and them, one pointed finger, and the plain inventory of what waits on the other side of the field and what it will do to the farm, the town, and the names on the rolls if the line doesn't hold. He doesn't raise his voice until the last sentence. A man who shouts the whole thing has nowhere to go at the end of it, and the end of it is where the men decide. He watches their faces do the deciding. That's the only poll he trusts.",
