    "story": "He has written it out fair and read it to the mirror, and the mirror was not impressed. Two minutes, the newspapers will say, as if the brevity were the point. Standing over the new graves with the flags still smelling of powder, he is not thinking about brevity. He is thinking about whether words can be load-bearing — whether a sentence can hold up a republic the way these men held up a line, and for how long, and at what cost per word. Four score and seven is not an opening. It's a measurement: of the distance between the promise and the bill. He raises his hand and begins paying.",
    "notes": "Depth does the staging: across the frame's bottom runs a blurred band of flag — red, white, and a single star, thrown out of focus in the immediate foreground — and the speaker rises sharp behind it, his stovepipe hat carrying the vertical to the top edge. His right hand is raised mid-argument, fingers curled on a point; the watch chain draws one fine line down the waistcoat. The ground is worked parchment, the surface at its most plate-like. For collectors: oratory composed in two depths — the nation soft in front, the voice hard behind it, and one curled hand doing the persuading.",
