    "story": "Be ready, boys is the whole of his religion, preached at whatever volume the smoke requires. Ready is not a state; it's a chore done in advance — canteen filled before the order, cartridge box full before the hunger, boots tied for a march nobody has announced. He has seen what unready looks like at the moment of the word, and he has buried some of it, and the preaching got louder after that. The boys mock the sermon in the ranks and repeat it to the new men word for word, which is how he knows it took. Readiness, like most true things, is just fear that got organized early.",
