    "story": "Ask him what it weighs and he'll tell you in pounds, because he has carried the inventory long enough to have it by heart: the rifle, the box, the blanket, the plate on his chest like a small shield over the heart. What he won't tell you is the other inventory, the one that accrues — the names that used to answer to his left and right, the letters he has written for men whose hands shook worse than his ever did. His own hands stay busy with the small work. Busy hands don't get asked questions. The weight distributes itself across a whole life if you keep moving, and he intends, God willing, to keep moving.",
