    "story": "The first sergeant's musket is mostly a pointer — at the gap in the line, at the man whose cartridge box hangs wrong, at the standard the whole company is supposed to become. He holds it upright now, bayonet fixed, and rests both hands on it like a man at a gate, watching his boys come up the road of the morning and doing the arithmetic that never appears in the returns: who's limping, who's lying about it, whose letter didn't come. The officers command the company. He carries it. There's a difference, and every private in the ranks can tell you exactly what it is, usually in the same words: the world, on one man's shoulders, at attention.",
