    "story": "The fight's done, the field's quiet, and the army — which has an order for everything — has not issued one for this. Now what is the soldier's oldest question, and it comes in flavors: now what do we eat, now what do we bury, now what do I write home that won't frighten the table. He leans on the rifle and lets the question do its rounds of the company. Somebody will answer it eventually; somebody always does, usually a sergeant, usually wrong in the details and right in the direction. Until then he stands the way men stand in doorways, armed and uncommitted, watching the smoke decide which way to drift.",
