    "story": "It ambushes him in the middle of nothing — a harness being mended, a pot coming to boil — and for a moment the camp goes quiet behind his closed eyes and there is a kitchen instead, and a laugh he could pick out of a fair crowd. He doesn't write the letters other men write. His are short because the long ones say the unsayable by accident. But thinking — thinking is uncensored, unpostmarked, and travels at no cost to anyone's worry. He stands there with his hands on his hips and a smile the sergeant would call idleness, conducting an entire conversation at the speed of love, which is faster than the mail and always has been.",
