    "story": "Camp is a country where words travel faster than horses and arrive with their uniforms changed. A rumor at breakfast is a fact by supper and a casualty list by Sunday, and the man who started it swears he only repeated what the cook heard from a teamster. So he has learned the arithmetic of speech the way he learned the manual: count before you fire. Letters get read aloud, and a careless sentence in one can do what a bullet couldn't — reach all the way home and wound in the kitchen. He holds his cup and his counsel in the same grip. Both are hot. Both spill if you wave them around.",
