    "story": "Riding drag is a job for somebody who can stand not knowing. Ahead of her the column raises a dust she can navigate by; behind her is everything the column has decided not to watch — the road they came down, the farm they passed at noon, and whatever might be following at the pace of a grudge. She checks it the way you check a door you already locked. Not because she expects it open. Because the one time you don't is the whole story of how columns disappear.",
